    "end": "Both came home wet.",
    "caption": "That's no moon in the first frame.\n\nPebb is a rock about forty kilometres across: one house, one resident, and a horizon you could walk to before lunch. Juno moved here for the quiet. Every morning she throws her ball east, has a long breakfast, and turns round to catch it coming in over the roof. She has never walked round to the far side. It isn't far.\n\nI threw my compass on my first morning, to check. It's still up there, next to her first ball.\n\nOn a rock this size, a throw of about 18 metres a second goes into orbit and comes round again in just under two hours. On Earth, you'd need nearly 8 kilometres a second.\n\nWould you throw two?"
  },
